    <briefdescription>
<para>Index entry with block compression support and shape information. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>On-disk portability: this descriptor and its <ref refid="structstar_1_1BlockInfo" kindref="compound">BlockInfo</ref> entries serialize their size_t fields as fixed-width little-endian uint64 values via write_u64 / read_u64 (which use the shift-based write_le/read_le, independent of host width and byte order). So .stards files interchange freely across platforms of any pointer width or endianness, including 32-bit wasm32 (size_t == 4 bytes) — the fields are narrowed to/from size_t with explicit static_casts on read. This matches the documented format-v1 layout. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
